1
00:00:01,148 --> 00:00:07,366
Dinner plans change. HestiaRelay helps you pick up where you left off.

2
00:00:07,366 --> 00:00:13,549
First: dinner for six on Friday, with a one hundred twenty dollar budget.

3
00:00:13,549 --> 00:00:19,737
Later, Ana's nut allergy joins the plan, in a completely new session.

4
00:00:19,737 --> 00:00:27,848
Are we ready for Friday? The guests, budget and allergy are remembered. Here's what
still needs attention.

5
00:00:27,848 --> 00:00:33,947
This is a deterministic Alexa Plus simulation, with no live Alexa connection.

6
00:00:33,947 --> 00:00:42,114
Before a sensitive decision, review the exact proposal. Approval belongs to these
details and this household context.

7
00:00:42,114 --> 00:00:49,531
Approval saves the decision. No purchase, payment, message or account change is made.

8
00:00:49,531 --> 00:00:57,914
Even after a real server restart, the three sessions, the plan and its approval are
still here.

9
00:00:57,914 --> 00:01:04,104
Lee is vegetarian. The plan changes, so it needs a new decision.

10
00:01:04,104 --> 00:01:11,377
Reject this proposal, and that decision stays with the household too. You're in
control.

11
00:01:11,377 --> 00:01:19,634
A real MCP client reads the same household over Streamable HTTP.

12
00:01:19,634 --> 00:01:27,840
HestiaRelay. One household, across separate conversations. Try the open source
project, and pick up where life left off.
